    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-6 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary mb-2">About the Author</h3>
      <div class="flex gap-4">
        
          <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ehmlvs/s3_images/refs/heads/main/elena.webp" alt="Elena Hmelovs" class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full">
        
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-primary">
            <a href="/founders/elena-hmelovs" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Elena Hmelovs</a>
          </h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted line-clamp-2">&lt;p&gt;Elena Hmelovs is a founder and operator who moved from venture investing into building products, and who now writes most of the review and interview output on Plain AI. She co-founded Big Layout Data, a proptech startup in the UAE, and since February 2026 has been the publication&#39;s most prolific author.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&#34;margin-top: 1.5em;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&#34;list-style: none; padding-left: 0;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ Co-founder and COO of Big Layout Data, a proptech startup that paired a database of apartment layouts with AI to recommend furniture sets matched to a specific floor plan, room size and budget. Andrejs Hmelovs was CEO.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ The company sold through furniture retailers and property platforms rather than to consumers directly, taking a share of purchases completed through its widget. The project is no longer operating.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ She was working out of Dubai&#39;s In5 Tech accelerator in 2022, where she met &lt;a href=&#34;/founders/olga-nayda&#34; style=&#34;color: #51A1E8; text-decoration: none;&#34;&gt;Olga Nayda&lt;/a&gt;, whom she later interviewed for Plain AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&#34;margin-top: 1.5em;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writing on Plain AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&#34;list-style: none; padding-left: 0;&#34;&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ Published 63 articles between 9 February and 13 August 2026, together drawing about 27,000 reads.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ The bulk of it is the Honest Review series — 44 pieces pricing and stress-testing individual tools, from &lt;a href=&#34;/tools/harvey&#34; style=&#34;color: #51A1E8; text-decoration: none;&#34;&gt;Harvey&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;/tools/lovable&#34; style=&#34;color: #51A1E8; text-decoration: none;&#34;&gt;Lovable&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href=&#34;/tools/deepseek&#34; style=&#34;color: #51A1E8; text-decoration: none;&#34;&gt;DeepSeek&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;/tools/canva-ai&#34; style=&#34;color: #51A1E8; text-decoration: none;&#34;&gt;Canva AI&lt;/a&gt;, each with pros, cons and alternatives rather than a verdict alone.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ Four Benchmark reports in August 2026 tested models on ordinary back-office work: invoice processing, expense verification, contract review and résumé screening.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ Seven Use Case pieces cover the practical edges of chatbot use — what your conversation history is worth as a data asset, what it exposes, and whether politeness costs tokens.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;✦ She also writes the Ai Talks interview series and news explainers, including a guide to the EU AI Act for startups outside Europe (8 June 2026).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&#34;margin-top: 1.5em;&#34;&gt;&lt;small&gt;Information accurate as of 22 September 2026.&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</p>
